<setup>
  <selectFromSequence name="k" from="3" to="6" step="1" exclude="5"/>
  <function name="f">cos(x)</function>
  <derivative name="fP">$f</derivative>
  <derivative name="fPP">$fP</derivative>
  <derivative name="fPPP">$fPP</derivative>
  <derivative name="fP4">$fPPP</derivative>
  <math name="a">pi/$k</math>

</setup>
<p>
  By responding to the following prompts, find the first several terms of the Taylor series of <me>f(x) = $f</me> centered at <m>a = \frac{\pi}{$k}</m>.
</p>

<p>
  <ol marker="a.">
    <li>
      <p>
        Complete the following table to assemble key information needed for the Taylor series of <m>f</m> centered at <m>a = \frac{\pi}{$k}</m>.  When you evaluate a trigonometric function at <m>a</m>, do so exactly.  For example, you might need to enter values such as <m>\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}</m> or <m>\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}</m>.
      </p>
        <tabular>
                <row>
                  <cell><m>f(x)=$f</m></cell>
                  <cell><m>f(\frac{\pi}{$k})=</m><answer>$$f($a)</answer></cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <cell><m>f'(x)=</m><answer>$fP</answer></cell>
                  <cell><m>f'(\frac{\pi}{$k})=</m><answer>$$fP($a)</answer></cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <cell><m>f''(x)=</m><answer>$fPP</answer></cell>
                  <cell><m>f''(\frac{\pi}{$k})=</m><answer>$$fPP($a)</answer></cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <cell><m>f'''(x)=</m><answer>$fPPP</answer></cell>
                  <cell><m>f'''(\frac{\pi}{$k})=</m><answer>$$fPPP($a)</answer></cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <cell><m>f^{(4)}(x)=</m><answer>$fP4</answer></cell>
                  <cell><m>f^{(4)}(\frac{\pi}{$k})=</m><answer>$$fP4($a)</answer></cell>
                </row>
              </tabular>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        State the first 5 terms of the Taylor series of <m>f</m> centered at <m>a = $a</m> by completing the blanks below; note that there is one blank per term and that several of the terms involve the variable <m>x</m>.
      </p>
      <p sectionWideCheckWork forceIndividualAnswerColoring>
        <m>T_f(x) = </m><answer>$$f($a)</answer><m>+</m><answer>$$fP($a)(x-$a)</answer><m>+</m><answer>$$fPP($a)/2! * (x-$a)^2</answer><m>+</m><answer>$$fPPP($a)/3! * (x-$a)^3</answer><m>+</m><answer>$$fP4($a)/4! * (x-$a)^4</answer><m>+ \cdots</m>
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</p>